# Development

The function is plain Node.js (${{ 'Node.js 22' if '22' in values.runtime else 'Node.js 24' }}, ES modules) with no
dependencies to install. The AWS SDK it uses for DynamoDB is part of the
Lambda runtime.

## Layout

| Path                    | Role                                                              |
| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `src/index.mjs`         | Lambda entry point (`index.handler`)                              |
| `src/routes.mjs`        | Route table: `"<METHOD> <path>"` to handler                       |
| `src/router.mjs`        | Routing, JSON responses, body parsing, error handling             |
{%- if values.enableCRUD %}
| `src/items/items.mjs`   | Handlers of the `/items` endpoints                                |
| `src/items/store.mjs`   | Items in the DynamoDB table named by `ITEMS_TABLE`                |
{%- endif %}
| `tests/`                | Unit tests (`node:test`), no AWS access needed                    |
| `scripts/package.sh`    | Writes `build/lambda.zip`                                         |

## Run the tests

```bash
npm test
```

## Build the deployment package

```bash
npm run package
```

This writes `build/lambda.zip`, the file `infra/` deploys. The pipeline does
the same through `.github/actions/build-lambda`.

## Implement an endpoint

API Gateway sends every request to the function with the method in
`event.httpMethod` and the path template in `event.resource` (for example
`/users/{id}`; the value of `{id}` is in `event.pathParameters.id`).
`src/routes.mjs` maps `"<METHOD> <path template>"` to a handler.

An endpoint requested when the repository was created starts as a stub that
answers `501`. Replace the stub with a handler:

```js
import { json, parseObject } from './router.mjs';

const createUser = async event => {
  const user = parseObject(event);
  return json(201, user);
};

export const routes = {
  // ...
  'POST /users': createUser,
};
```

Throw `new HttpError(status, message)` from `router.mjs` to answer with an
error status. Anything else that is thrown is logged and answered with `500`.

To add an endpoint that was not requested at creation, add it to `endpoints`
in `infra/terraform.tfvars.json` as well, so that API Gateway routes it; see
[Operations](operations.md#change-the-configuration).
